course: dictionary
lesson: 14365
title: Opposed: against or opposite
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Opposed» is the past form of «oppose», which means to be against something. «The villagers opposed the plan» means they said no to it and worked against it.
explain: When you are «opposed to» something, you disagree with it. «Mum is opposed to sweets before dinner» tells you she does not want them then. Look for the word «to» after it: it often shows the thing people are against.
explain: «Opposed» can also mean very different. Hot and cold are opposed ideas, so they are opposites. «As opposed to» compares two things: «She likes walking, as opposed to running» shows that walking and running are different choices.
fact: Opposed is the past form of oppose: «They opposed the plan» means they were against it.
fact: If you are opposed to something, you are against it.
fact: Opposed things are very different or opposite to each other.
fact: «Strongly opposed» and «bitterly opposed» show that someone is against something very much.
fact: «As opposed to» contrasts two things, like «weight as opposed to mass».
exercise: «The villagers opposed the plan to build a new road.» What does opposed mean here? | Were happy with it | Painted the road | Ignored the map | *Were against it
exercise: Mum says, «I am opposed to sweets before dinner.» What does opposed to mean? | Asleep after lunch | Keen on, so she wants more | Allergic to them | *Against, so she says no
exercise: «Hot and cold are opposed ideas.» What does opposed mean here? | Very loud | Almost the same | *Very different, like opposites | Hard to see
test: «She likes walking, as opposed to running.» What does as opposed to show? | A time of day | Something that is missing | Two things that are the same | *Two things being compared as different
test: Which phrase shows someone is against something very strongly? | Mildly curious | Kindly helpful | Fast asleep | *Bitterly opposed
exam: Which word is the past form of oppose? | Opposing | Opposite | *Opposed | Opposes
